  {
    "index": 9,
    "hash": "vQQCt5FdhlZCaOhCJ5+2sGEokn8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T15:46:23.310Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Powerhouse Design System is a collection of reusable front-end components based on GraphQL scalars. It provides:\n\n- Consistent UI components across Powerhouse applications\n- Automatic inclusion as a dependency in new projects\n- Customization via CSS variables\n- Custom scalar types tailored for the web3 ecosystem\n\nBuilt-in GraphQL scalars: `String`, `Int`, `Float`, `Boolean`, `ID`\nPowerhouse custom scalars: `OID` (Object ID), `Currency`, `DateTime`, and other web3-specific types\n\nThese scalars are more than just type definitions - they are linked to reusable front-end components from the `@powerhousedao/document-engineering` package. When you use a custom scalar in your schema, corresponding UI components are available for rendering and editing that data type.\n\n## Precision on naming and location\n\n\"Design System\" is loose here: `@powerhousedao/design-system` and `@powerhousedao/document-engineering` are **two different packages** \u2014 the former lives in the powerhouse monorepo (`packages/design-system`), the latter is an independently versioned external repo. The scalar-backed components described above come from document-engineering.\n\nThe scalar definitions live in `src/scalars/graphql/` of that repo, one file per scalar. `OID.ts`, `Currency.ts` and `DateTime.ts` are all present, alongside `Amount`, `AmountCrypto`, `AmountCurrency`, `AmountFiat`, `AmountMoney`, `AmountPercentage`, `AmountTokens`, `Date`, `EmailAddress`, `EthereumAddress`, `OLabel`, `PHID`, `URL` and `File`. Their UI counterparts split across three subpaths: `/scalars` (form fields), `/ui` (layout) and `/table`.\n\n_Source-verified 2026-08-13 against the document-engineering repo at v1.40.5 (`/home/p/Powerhouse/document-engineering`), a separate repo from the powerhouse monorepo._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T15:46:20.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T15:46:23.310Z"
    }
  },
